{"id":"CVE-2010-4478","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2010-12-06T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-05-28T18:51:30.518Z","description":"OpenSSH 5.6 and earlier, when J-PAKE is enabled, does not properly validate the public parameters in the J-PAKE protocol, which allows remote attackers to bypass the need for knowledge of the shared secret, and successfully authenticate, by sending crafted values in each round of the protocol, a related issue to CVE-2010-4252.","cwe":["n/a","CWE-287 CWE-287 Improper Authentication"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":9.8,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/jpake.c#rev1.5","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://kb.juniper.net/InfoCenter/index?page=content&id=JSA10673","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://oval.cisecurity.org/repository/search/definition/oval%3Aorg.mitre.oval%3Adef%3A12338","tags":["vdb-entry","signature","x_refsource_OVAL"],"name":"oval:org.mitre.oval:def:12338"},{"url":"http://www.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/jpake.c.diff?r1=1.4%3Br2=1.5%3Bf=h","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/seb-m/jpake","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=659297","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://seb.dbzteam.org/crypto/jpake-session-key-retrieval.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-4755","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2011-03-02T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T03:55:34.968Z","description":"The (1) remote_glob function in sftp-glob.c and the (2) process_put function in sftp.c in OpenSSH 5.8 and earlier, as used in FreeBSD 7.3 and 8.1, NetBSD 5.0.2, OpenBSD 4.7, and other products, allow remote authenticated users to cause a denial of service (CPU and memory consumption) via crafted glob expressions that do not match any pathnames, as demonstrated by glob expressions in SSH_FXP_STAT requests to an sftp daemon, a different vulnerability than CVE-2010-2632.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://cvsweb.netbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb.cgi/src/crypto/dist/ssh/Attic/sftp.c#rev1.21.6.1","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://securityreason.com/achievement_securityalert/89","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SREASONRES"],"name":"20101007 Multiple Vendors libc/glob(3) resource exhaustion (+0day remote ftpd-anon)"},{"url":"http://securityreason.com/exploitalert/9223","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://cvsweb.netbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb.cgi/src/crypto/dist/ssh/Attic/sftp-glob.c#rev1.13.12.1","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://cxib.net/stuff/glob-0day.c","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/security/advisories/NetBSD-SA2010-008.txt.asc","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_NETBSD"],"name":"NetBSD-SA2010-008"},{"url":"http://securityreason.com/securityalert/8116","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SREASON"],"name":"8116"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-5107","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2013-03-07T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-05-29T20:32:32.155Z","description":"The default configuration of OpenSSH through 6.1 enforces a fixed time limit between establishing a TCP connection and completing a login, which makes it easier for remote attackers to cause a denial of service (connection-slot exhaustion) by periodically making many new TCP connections.","cwe":["n/a","CWE-400 CWE-400 Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":7.5,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/servconf.c?r1=1.234#rev1.234","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2013-1591.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2013:1591"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=144050155601375&w=2","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"HPSBMU03409"},{"url":"http://www.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/sshd_config?r1=1.89#rev1.89","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=908707","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/58162","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"58162"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/topics/security/linuxbulletinjan2016-2867209.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/topics/security/cpujan2015-1972971.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/sshd_config.5?r1=1.156#rev1.156","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2013/02/07/3","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[